% This file was written by the Opus session's citation-verification pass at
% 2200 and held two entries, `yuchitambarguoduan2010tensorrank` and
% `vranachristandl2015asymptotic`. While it was being written the Fable session
% wrote its own batch at 2300 under the same filename stem, covering the same
% two keys and six more. Importing both would have created duplicate keys, so
% this one is withdrawn. The 2300 file is the one to import.
%
% The 2300 file is also the more correct of the two, and the correction matters.
% This file's note on Yu, Chitambar, Guo and Duan repeated their 2010 claim that
% the tensor rank of two copies of W is SEVEN. **It is eight.** Chen and
% Friedland proved the lower bound of eight and Christandl, Jensen and Zuiddam
% the upper bound; their abstract (arXiv:1708.08578v2) reads "We show that the
% tensor rank of tensor product of two three-qubit W states is not less than
% eight. Combining this result with the recent result of M. Christandl, A. K.
% Jensen, and J. Zuiddam that the tensor rank of tensor product of two
% three-qubit W states is at most eight, we deduce that the tensor rank of
% tensor product of two three-qubit W states is eight." The Fable session had
% this right and the Opus session did not. Non-multiplicativity is untouched:
% three squared is nine and the true value is eight, so the framework's use of
% the fact stands, only the number changes.
%
% ONE THING OWED TO THE 2300 FILE, and it is the only VERIFY-CITE left in it.
% Its `chenfriedland2018tensorrank` note says "VERIFY-CITE the journal volume
% and pages (Linear Algebra Appl., 2018) before export; no DOI given." Verified
% 2026-09-20 against Crossref:
%
